+# Cloudflare runtime guide
+
+Before deployment, the Worker owner must export each registered AIChatAgent class and declare its Cloudflare Durable Object binding. The migration owner must add the corresponding classes to a versioned SQLite Durable Object migration (`new_sqlite_classes` for their first deployment) and maintain later rename or deletion migrations without rewriting deployed history.
+
+The provider owner must configure the binding or secret required by the AI SDK provider selected for `openai/gpt-5`; the model string alone does not prove a provider binding or credential name. The deployment owner must supply the Worker entrypoint and routes, apply the bindings and migration in Worker configuration, provision provider credentials, validate in the target Cloudflare environment, and deploy the Worker.
+
+This repository contains no Worker configuration or entrypoint, so static inspection does not prove the Durable Object binding names, migration tag, provider binding, routes, credentials, or deployed state.
